{"name":"Carrara","hex":"#eeebe4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Carrara","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from Italian.","A town in Massa Carrara, Tuscany, Italy, famous for its marble quarries"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Carrara"}],"entries":[{"title":"Carrara","blocks":[{"text":"Carrara is a town and comune in Tuscany, in central Italy, of the province of Massa and Carrara, and notable for the white or blue-grey marble quarried there. It is on the Carrione River, some 100 kilometres (62 mi) west-northwest of Florence. Its motto is Latin: \"Fortitudo mea in rota\", a reference firstly to the marble shipping industry from Roman times onwards."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Carrara%2C_veduta_verso_il_centro_storico%2C_avenza_e_il_mare_da_via_salita_sponda_04.jpg/330px-Carrara%2C_veduta_verso_il_centro_storico%2C_avenza_e_il_mare_da_via_salita_sponda_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carrara"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Carrara.PNG/500px-Carrara.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Carrara.PNG/1280px-Carrara.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Carrara.PNG/500px-Carrara.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"View of Carrara","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarrara.PNG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Cararia.jpg/500px-Cararia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Cararia.jpg/1280px-Cararia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parse